# PHASE 7 — COLLECTION STATUS POPUP

Review and integrate the existing collection progress popup.

When a conversation is being collected or backfilled, display a temporary status card.

The popup should:

- Identify the conversation being processed.
- Display collection status.
- Display progress where progress can be accurately measured.
- Display collected message counts.
- Display relevant errors.
- Display collection status transitions.
- Provide cancellation where supported.
- Avoid blocking the Discord interface.
- Automatically disappear after completion with an appropriate brief completion indication.
- Handle interrupted collection.
- Handle failed collection.
- Handle retries.

Do not fabricate progress percentages.

Use meaningful status states.

Examples:

- Waiting.
- Collecting.
- Processing.
- Completed.
- Interrupted.
- Failed.
- Cancelled.

## Initial backfill behavior

The initial historical backfill must occur only once per conversation, according to the persisted collection state.

- Persist collection state using stable conversation identifiers.
- Distinguish never-collected conversations from collected conversations.
- Distinguish completed from incomplete collections.
- Avoid repeatedly restarting full historical collection on every visit.
- Reuse previously collected data.
- Perform lightweight incremental collection when supported.
- Resume or retry incomplete collection appropriately.
- Do not falsely report complete historical coverage.
- Preserve deduplication and persistence integrity.

The popup must accurately reflect the collection engine's actual state.

